  <p>The listening topic picked up <strong>57,664 mentions</strong> in September, up from 11,753 in August. Almost all of that growth came from the 25th anniversary of 9/11: 47,767 September mentions (83%) referenced the attacks, mostly remembrances of American Airlines Flights 11 and 77 on X. Those posts match the topic because they mention American Airlines and its pilots, not because they discuss APA.</p>
  <p>Set 9/11 aside and the conversation about American&rsquo;s pilots, their contract and the company&rsquo;s leadership held roughly steady (3,362 mentions vs. 3,643 in August), while its tone improved. Negative mentions fell from 24% of that conversation to 15%. It peaked on Sept 17, the day after Capt. Silva&rsquo;s comments to <em>The Dallas Morning News</em>.</p>
